with clipboards but supporters say the  vouchers were a success giving some  political clout to even the poorest and  making candidates take notice we did see  Canada  campaigning in ways that they not  campaigned in the past we did see them  not sitting in a conference room dialing  for dollars but out you know pounding  the pavement the program is very  expensive candidates receive 1.1 million  dollars in voucher money but it cost  over a million dollars to run a high sum  for a system that did create many more  campaign donors but by the city's own  data only drove up the price tag to  getting elected brett dan springer in  seattle dan thanks
 

